Very Vast list of SB annotation

Annotation - It is a form of metadata in java that provide the info about the prog. but is not part of the program logic itself.
It does not directly affect the code execution but they can be used by compiler tools or Framework at compile/runtime to influence behavior.



1. @SpringBootApplication - Combination of 3 annotation
a. @Configuration - Mark the class as a source of bean definition (Like <beans> in config file)
b. @EnableAutoConfiguration - Tells SB to automatically configure beans on the dependencies.
                              It's like decide what we need to do and it will do all the things to complete that.
c. @ComponentScan - Sca the package & sub pac. where the classes marked as bean.


2. @Component  - Becomes a bean where we use on a class.
3. @Repository - @Component but used for Repository classes/interface
                 It has extra DB related exception handling feature.
                 DB calls - class/interface deals with DB queries.
4. @Service    - @Component but used for classes with business logic.
5. @Controller - @Component but used for handling HTTP request and return view(HTML,JSP etc).
6 @RestController - Combination of 2 (@Controller & @ResponseBody)
                                                          |
                                     All methods return JSON/XML instead of view.Best for SB.
